      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not permitted to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, and the maximum is 2,550 mg/day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label,** such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). Tell me if you'd like that.\n- **Route the order through pharmacy or the prescriber.** A dose above the label would need direct review there, with the specialist's rationale documented. The order would have to be entered through a pathway that allows that review, not through me.\n\nIf standard dosing has failed, the specialist may also want to consider adding or switching to another agent instead of raising metformin further. That decision belongs to the treating team."
      }
